<hr class="solid">

<div>

    <h2>Projects</h2>
    <div class="project-grid">

        <Project
                title="Senior Research Project"
                description="A research project into using machine learning to see if one could algorithmically predict
                what the best way to brew a cup of coffee is based on the bean origin, altitude, and other factors."
                tags={["Machine Learning", "Python", "Linear Algebra"]}
        />
        <Project
                title="Lotus 58 Custom Keyboard"
                description="I've always enjoyed building mechanical keyboards, but always wanted to build something
                completely mine from the ground up. The Lotus 58 is a custom split keyboard that I build over the course
                of a couple weeks to learn more about how electronics work, as it's built entirely from scratch (including
                printing the PCBs yourself. I built mine with Gateron Silent Ink Black v2 switches, so I could code/write
                late into the night."
                tags={[""]}
        />

        <Project
                title="Gostow"
                description="GNU Stow is a very popular utility that is used by both Linux and macOS users to manage &quot;dotfiles&quot;
                (configuration files which are stored as text inside a special folder). However, GNU Stow was originally
                written to help software developers build and test their programs, so managing dotfiles wasn't their original
                goal, resulting in many workarounds having to be done in order for dotfile management to work. I wrote Gostow
                as a standalone replacement which specializes only in dotfile management, which was written entirely in Go."
                tags={["Go"]}
        />

        <Project
                title="Zettk-CLI"
                description="A CLI tool I developed to help with my note taking system (that being the Zettlekasten system popularized by Leibniz)
		       without the need for external GUI tools such as Obsidian. It worked by auto creating and linking notes together as I
		       create them, building the web of notes as I learn. This system hooks directly into your Neovim configuration as well,
		       enabling a fast, dynamic workflow of note taking that prioritizes getting knowledge down without the hassle of using
		       a GUI application."
                tags={["Go", "CLI"]}
        />
    </div>

    <hr class="solid">

    <Education/>

</div>
